{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation"],"declarations":445,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.pure_gg_reading3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.pure_gg_reading3","kind":"theorem","line":2021,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.lean#L2021-L2041","doc":"**Main theorem.** Every pure γγ word of length `m ≥ 1` on four strands passes reading 3\n(all level characters `≥ 0`) for `1 ≤ q ≤ 1 + (1/12)/m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.levelChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.levelChar","kind":"def","line":2004,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.lean#L2004-L2019","doc":"Level character `χ_{(m,μ)}(w) = Σ_λ (y_λ / y_μ) Σ_{T ↓ m = μ} W^λ_{TT}`, with the\nGelfand–Tsetlin tableaux ordered as in the seminormal matrices: on `(3,1)` the entry `4`, `3`, `2`\nsits in the second row; on `(2,2)` the second row is `{3,4}`, then `{2,4}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.LevelShape.l1_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.GammaGammaFourStrandPureBound.LevelShape.l1_1","kind":"ctor","line":2002,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/GammaGammaFourStra